12) Among the following statements:

(i) $3^{10}$ is a cube;

(ii) $3^{10}$ is odd;

(iii) $3^{10}$ is a square;

which ones are correct?
(A) Only (i)
(B) only (ii)
(C) only (iii)
(D) (ii) and (iii)
(E) all three.

\section*{Problem 3A - 201043A}

Determine all pairs \((x ; y)\) of real numbers with \(y>0\) and \(y \neq 1\), for which the following system of equations (1), (2) is satisfied!

\[
\begin{aligned}
x \log _{y}(\sqrt{3}-\sqrt{2})^{x} & =2 \log _{y}(5-\sqrt{24}) \\
y-x & =2
\end{aligned}
\]
